# A [[contest]] [[between]] [[people]], [[animals]], [[vehicles]], etc. where the [[goal]] is to be the [[first]] to [[reach]] some [[objective]]. Example: Several horses run in a ''horse race'', and the first one to reach the finishing post wins
#: {{ux|en|The '''race''' around the [[park]] was won by Johnny, who ran faster than the others.}}
#: {{ux|en|We had a '''race''' to see who could [[finish]] the book the [[quickest]].}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Ecclesiastes|9|11|text=I returned, and saw vnder the Sunne, That the '''race''' is not to the swift, nor the battell to the strong, neither yet bread to the wise, nor yet riches to men of vnderstanding, nor yet fauour to men of skil; but time and chance happeneth to them all.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en |date=November 2, 2012 |title=After Days of Pressure, Marathon Is Off |journal=The New York Times |author=Ken Belson |url=http://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/sports/new-york-city-marathon-will-not-be-held-sunday.html |text=After days of intensifying pressure from runners, politicians and the general public to call off the New York City Marathon in the wake of Hurricane Sandy, city officials and the event’s organizers decided Friday afternoon to cancel the '''race'''.}}
# Swift [[progress]]; [[rapid]] [[motion]]; an instance of moving or driving at high speed.
#* {{RQ:Bacon Sylva Sylvarum|passage=The flight of many birds is swifter than the '''race''' of any beasts.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[race condition]].
# A [[progressive]] [[movement]] toward a goal.
#: {{ux|en|the '''race''' to cure cancer}}<!--is this what this sense is intended to cover??-->
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1624|first=Francis|last=Bacon|editor=Basil Montagu|chapter=Considerations Touching a War with Spain|title=The Works of Francis Bacon|volume=5|publisher=William Pickering
|year_published=1826|page=240|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/worksfrancisbac12conggoog/page/240|text=An offensive war is made, which is unjust in the aggressor; the prosecution and '''race''' of the war carrieth the defendant to invade the ancient patrimony of the first aggressor, who is now turned defendant; shall he sit down, and not put himself in defence?}}
# A [[fast-moving]] [[current]] of water, such as that which [[powers]] a [[mill]] [[wheel]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1893|chapter=Remarks upon the Way from Abingdon to Southamption, and other Places|title=The Manuscripts of His Grace the Duke of Portland|volume=2|location=London|publisher=Her Majesty's Stationery Office|page=288|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=1asKAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA288|text=Here are in these seas two dangerous '''races''', the one called St. Alban's, the other Portland Race.}}
# A water channel, especially one built to lead water to or from a point where it is utilised.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1957-12-16|first=A. H.|last=Mouat|first2=R. C.|last2=Stuart|first3=G.|last3=Mason|title=Farming in Ida Valley, Central Otago|journal=The New Zealand Journal of Agriculture|volume=95|number=6|page=587|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=VrnxRUx9kuUC&pg=RA1-PA587|text=Water for irrigation is stored in the high country behind the Upper Manorburn Dam.  Two parallel '''races''' at different levels run along the west side of the valley and one '''race''' flowing along the east side is supplemented by water stored at the Poolburn Dam.}}
# Competitive action of any kind, especially when prolonged; hence, [[career]]; course of life.
#: {{synonyms|en|course|progress}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Regained|book=Samson Agonistes|40|line=598|passage=My '''race''' of glory run, and '''race''' of ſhame,}}
# A [[ring]] with a [[groove]] in which rolling elements (such as balls) ride, forming part of a rolling-element [[bearing]] (for example, a [[ball bearing]]).
#* {{quote-book|en|date=1965-08-15|title=Maintenance of Aeronautical Antifriction Bearings|others=NAVWEPS 01-1A-503|publisher=United States Bureau of Naval Weapons
|section=section 2|page=5|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=M861fCPQGssC&pg=PA5|text=These bearings do not employ a loading groove or filling slot but utilize an uninterrupted '''race''' groove containing the maximum number of balls that can be introduced by eccentric displacement of the '''races'''.  Due to the relatively large size of the balls and the fact that the ball curvature is only slightly less than the '''race''' curvature, the bearings have comparatively high load carrying capacity in both axial and radial directions.}}

