##* {{quote-book|en|year=1799|first=Joshua|last=Rowlin|title=The Complete Cow-Doctor; Or, Farmer's Companion|location=London|edition=2nd|page=42|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=vHdZAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA42|text=They have another breed, called the Dunlop cows, which are allowed to be the best '''race''' for yielding milk in Great Britain or Ireland, not only for large quantities, but also for richness in quality.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1875|title=The Living World|first=Augustus C. L.|last=Arnold|volume=1|page=88|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=jasaAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA88|location=Boston|publisher=Samuel Walker & Co|text=Great St. Bernard Dog—This '''race''' is nearly allied to the Newfoundland Dog in form, stature, hair, and colors; but the head and ears are like that of a Water Spaniel.}}
